@startuml
title Cycles as statechart transitions: revisit, bound, yield, scope self-loop
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "Plain revisit" as Frag1 #E9F5EA {
  state "Draft" as F1A #DCEEFF
  state "Critique" as F1B #DCEEFF
  F1A --> F1B : completed
  F1B --> F1A : needsWork\n(re-entry, no entry/exit actions)
}

state "Bounded self-loop" as Frag2 #DCEEFF {
  state "Refine" as F2A #DCEEFF
  F2A --> F2A : again [<latex>\kappa_c(e) < b_e</latex>]\n/ <latex>\kappa_c(e){+}{+}</latex>
  state "Fallback" as F2B #FFE0C8
  F2A --> F2B : iterationLimit\n(disposition rewritten at the SOURCE node,\nnot a traversal; exactly <latex>b_e</latex> traversals occur)
}

state "Durable-yield transition" as Frag3 #FFF0D9 {
  state "Analyze" as F3A #DCEEFF
  state "Parked at target\nyield:{token}:{transition}\ndueAt = park instant" as F3B #F8DADA
  F3A --> F3B : loop.durableYield\n/ checkpoint and suspend (durableYield);\ntoken pre-positioned at the target,\nno transitionTaken emitted
  state "Target (Enter phase)" as F3C #DCEEFF
  F3B --> F3C : timerFired [exact deadline]\nby the recovery scheduler
}

state "Scope-node self-loop" as Frag4 #E7DCF5 {
  state "ReviewScope (composite)" as F4A #FFF0D9
  F4A --> F4A : rejected\n/ full exit: snapshot history, exit activities;\nfull re-entry: entry activities, restore
}

note right of Frag3 #EAF7EE
The yield parks already due, so the recovery
scheduler resumes it automatically through the
same self-signed timerFired path as a due timer:
one ledger round-trip per iteration, Enter-phase
re-entry at the target.
end note
note bottom of Frag2 #EAF7EE
Counters live in token context, so concurrent branches
and separate invocations never share a budget, and the
count survives suspension, checkpointing, and history.
end note
@enduml
